  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 124 PM MDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nWarmer and dry conditions remain in the offing through the weekend, as drier\nair within modest north to northwest flow aloft works back into the region,\nas upper level ridging builds back across the Great Basin and into the \nRockies. Temperatures warm back into the 70s to low 80s across the plains on \nSaturday with slowly cooler temperatures in the offing for Sunday, as passing\nwave across the northern Rockies sends a weak front across the plains. Highs \nacross the higher terrain remain in the 50s and 60s through the weekend.  \nWill need to continue to monitor high valley lows, as warming aloft\nshould keep lows above freezing, however, can't rule out the potential \nfor patchy frost. \n\nLatest models continue to indicate the upper ridge flattening across the region\nwith a few occasional disturbances within the stronger flow in place across the \nNorthern Tier, to bring occasional chances for precipitation through the middle \nto end of the work week, with temperatures remaining at to slightly above \nseasonal norms through the week.",
